  - { name: "Invulnerabilities", description: "Impervious to vacuum, poisonous and toxic atmospheres, toxins, drugs and radiation. Reduced to zero M.D.C. a machine person falls into a coma and repairs itself at 10 M.D.C. per twenty minutes until it is conscious again at 20 M.D.C.; further repair needs metal to eat. It can take damage to 99 points below zero and survive. At -100 M.D.C. it is utterly destroyed." }
  - { name: "Resistant to Magic and Psionics", description: "No magic and no psionic powers of its own, but highly resistant to both - the +4 vs magic and +3 vs psionics in the class bonuses." }
  - { name: "Internal Fusion Power Plant", description: "Self-repairing through the nano-machines, so it lasts as long as the machine person does - 200 years or more. When the character dies the plant goes inert." }
  - { name: "Horror Factor", description: "10, entirely on reputation and entirely undeserved. A number the machine person projects, which the sheet has no field for." }
  - { name: "Average Life Span", description: "Brain waves decay after about 200 years of use, and death follows in 1D6 years. No cure has ever been found - possibly a Machinist measure against overpopulation." }
  - { name: "Size", description: "Varies, but tends to stay at five to seven feet (1.5 to 2.1 m) and around 300 lbs (135 kg). A humanoid with metallic skin, no hair, in silver, gray, red or blue. The living alloy is smooth and soft like flesh, but cool - people compare it to a snake." }
special_abilities:
  - name: "Morphing"
    description: "Given raw metal or M.D.C. alloy to infect with nano-machines and meld into itself, a machine person can rebuild parts of its body. Each change takes 1D6 melee rounds to make and the same to reverse. ARMOR: meld with metal for up to 1D4x100 M.D.C., growing 2D6 inches (5 to 30 cm) and 1D6x100 lbs (45 to 272 kg) - not usable inside a fighter, a robot vehicle or power armor. STRENGTH: reshape and add metal for +10 to P.S. COMPRESSION: halve height and width by crushing the internal parts together (a grotesque process, Horror Factor 12 to anyone unfamiliar with it), extend limbs to three times their length, or narrow the whole body enough to slide through bars. WEAPON MELD: meld with a sword or axe for +1 to strike and parry with it."
  - name: "Machine Melding"
    description: "Cables extrude from the limbs and take control of any machine they can reach, bypassing its controls entirely. Melding takes 1D6 melee rounds; once it succeeds the machine person is the overriding force in control and cannot be subverted or cut out. It grants +15% to all piloting rolls, +1 to strike, parry and dodge with the vehicle, and the equivalent of Robot, Power Armor and Piloting Combat: ELITE with it - plus the equivalent of a universal headjack and +15% to all computer operation, programming and hacking rolls. Anti-intrusion systems on some vehicles force a save vs psionics or take 2D6 M.D. and fail the meld."
  - name: "Regeneration of Power and Energy"
    description: "Through the melding power, a machine person can recharge energy weapons indefinitely."
  - name: "Regeneration and Nutrition"
    description: "It does not eat in the humanoid sense, but wear and damage are repaired by consuming metal - 2.5 lbs (1 kg) to replace 1D6 M.D.C., plus a similar amount weekly to stay in trim. A month with no metal costs 1D6 M.D.C. A healthy machine person regenerates 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, up to twenty times in twenty-four hours, without eating anything extra."
  - name: "Reproduction"
    description: "Once a year a male and female can mate and produce one young, and their programming makes the urge as intense as it is in anything born. After a building period of 1D6 months the female releases a baby robot with 1D4x10 M.D.C., which she loses from her own total until it regrows. The child''s development takes 2D4 years and is genuinely a childhood: physical skills build its speed and muscle, schooling builds its knowledge, exactly as they would for a living creature."
skills:
  occ_skills:
